---
import BlogPostLayout from '@layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';
import { getPost } from '@lib/blog';

const post = getPost('asial-sydney-2024');
---
<BlogPostLayout post={post}>
  <p class="lead">
    A short recap of the 2024 ASIAL Security Conference &amp;
    Exhibition at ICC Sydney : and the moment a visiting
    technician walked off with the title of <strong>Fastest Tech in
    Sydney</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>The expo</h2>

  <p>
    We had a fantastic time at the 2024 ASIAL Security Conference &amp;
    Exhibition at ICC Sydney. Three days, the entire NSW security
    industry under one roof, and a lot of conversations about where
    integrated commercial security is heading over the next five years.
  </p>

  <p>
    For us, the standout themes from the floor were the maturing of
    cloud-managed access control for commercial sites, the noticeable
    jump in AI analytics actually delivering on the marketing pitch
    (rather than mostly producing false-positive alerts), and a
    long-overdue convergence of monitoring platforms with the same
    operator console.
  </p>

  <h2>The Fastest Tech in Sydney challenge</h2>

  <p>
    A big highlight was our &ldquo;Fastest Tech in Sydney&rdquo;
    challenge at the Ktronics stand. Visiting technicians and aspiring
    apprentices took turns running a timed practical task. The winning
    technician completed it in an impressive
    <strong>2 minutes and 10 seconds</strong>.
  </p>

  <p>
    A pretty solid number to beat at SecTech 2026 next May, if any
    Australian techs reading this are up for the challenge.
  </p>

  <p>
    Thank you to everyone who visited our stand and took part. If you
    want to catch us at the next event, we&apos;re exhibiting at the
    <a href="/resources/blog/sectech-roadshow-2026/">SecTech Roadshow 2026</a>
    across five Australian cities this May.
  </p>
</BlogPostLayout>
